## 3. Validation checklist

Run on the **Target** unless noted.

**While NAT is still connected:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `apt list --upgradable 2>/dev/null \| tail -n +2` | Empty |
| 2 | `test -f /var/run/reboot-required && echo YES \|\| echo NO` | `NO` |
| 3 | `apt-config dump \| grep -E 'Periodic::(Update-Package-Lists\|Unattended-Upgrade)'` | Both set to `"1"` |
| 4 | `sudo unattended-upgrade --dry-run --debug 2>&1 \| grep 'Allowed origins'` | Includes `-security` |
| 5 | `systemctl list-timers 'apt-daily*'` | Both timers present |

**Users and roles:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 6 | `id secadmin; id operator1` | `secadmin` in `lab-admins` and **not** in `sudo`; `operator1` in `lab-operators` |
| 7 | `getent passwd labadmin` | No output |
| 8 | `sudo passwd -S root` | `root L ...` (still locked) |
| 9 | `stat -c '%a %n' /home/secadmin /etc/sudoers.d/*` | `750` for the home; `440` for each sudoers file |
| 10 | `sudo visudo -c` | `parsed OK` for all files |

**As `secadmin`:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 11 | `sudo whoami` | Asks for the password, prints `root` |

**As `operator1`:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 12 | `sudo -l` | Lists only the three allowed commands |
| 13 | `su -` | `su: Permission denied` |
| 14 | `sudo systemctl status ssh --no-pager` | Allowed |
| 15 | `sudo apt update` ; `sudo -i` ; `sudo cat /etc/shadow` ; `sudo systemctl status ssh` (no `--no-pager`) | **All denied**, because they don't match the rules exactly. The last one is deliberate. |

**After disconnecting NAT:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 16 | `ip route` | **No default route** |
| 17 | `ping -c 1 -W 2 1.1.1.1` | Fails (network unreachable) |
| 18 | On the Bastion: `ping -c 3 10.10.10.20` | 0% loss (lab network still works) |

If you want evidence for the README, pipe outputs into `~/evidence/p03.txt` on the machine you're on. Do not record passwords.
